   "finding": "Theme saves no longer scale with the checkpoint (6.4 MiB: 5.15 ms, max 15.06 -> about 1.7-2.0 ms); duplicates are 2-3x faster (6.4 MiB: 49 -> 21 ms); database files are half the size because theme saves no longer strand a checkpoint copy. Checkpoint writes, appends and opening are unchanged within run-to-run variance (6.4 MiB checkpoint write 38 ms before, 39-45 ms across three runs after)."
  },
  "structuralBatches": {
   "command": "cargo run --locked --release -p hitslop-core --example core_cost",
   "thousandInsertBatchMS": {
    "1000": 27.63,
    "5000": 36.66
   },
   "decision": "Accepted; no change to publication.rs. 1,000 moves is the largest batch allowed, and its worst case is 24 ms (restore at 5,000 rows). The per-row order search accounts for about 9 ms of that (14.7 ms at 1,000 rows vs 23.7 ms at 5,000). Publishing the whole list instead would give every row in the page a new identity and re-render them all, costing more than it saves.",
   "invalidatedThousandMoveBatchMS": {
